# RestoreGuard — crontab entry.
#
# Install with:   crontab -e
# Check with:     crontab -l
# Remove with:    crontab -r
#
# This verifies the backup every 30 minutes. cron runs with a minimal
# environment (no shell profile), so every path here is absolute and the
# Postgres client is pinned by PG_CLIENT_BIN inside the project's .env.
#
# Local macOS (current machine):
*/30 * * * * cd /Users/tejaskunta/RestoreGuard && .venv/bin/python -m restoreguard.verify >> logs/cron.log 2>&1

# On EC2 the project path differs — adjust the `cd` target, e.g.:
# */30 * * * * cd /opt/restoreguard && .venv/bin/python -m restoreguard.verify >> logs/cron.log 2>&1